1
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:47,860
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,970
[Episode 15]

3
00:01:51,509 --> 00:01:53,150
Come on, we are Wudiren!

4
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:53,920
I'm Renke.

5
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,640
I'm Mao.

6
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,150
Right.

7
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:56,680
We'll put on

8
00:01:57,229 --> 00:01:58,750
3 shows in a row

9
00:01:58,789 --> 00:01:59,840
in Shapu Village.

10
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,200
Be there or be square!

11
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,640
Be there or be square!

12
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,480
Okay, bye!

13
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,120
Retake.

14
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:05,750
Come here.

15
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,760
Don't block me.

16
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,310
Retake.

17
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:07,760
Okay.

18
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:09,050
Come on. Ready?

19
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,889
Come on, ready, action!

20
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,870
Let me speak first. Come on.

21
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:13,200
Okay.

22
00:02:13,590 --> 00:02:14,590
Hello, everyone.

23
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,680
Wonderful night!

24
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,000
We are the Wudiren.

25
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,870
I'm Renke.

26
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:18,960
I'm Mao.

27
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:19,560
Right.

28
00:02:19,590 --> 00:02:20,590
Remember, in Shapu Village...

29
00:02:20,590 --> 00:02:21,840
In Shapu Village...

30
00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:23,130
Take a look!

31
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:25,360
Take a look!

32
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,150
Sir, open the door!

33
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,200
Open the door! Wudiren!

34
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:36,190
Wudiren!

35
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,030
Wudiren's concert!

36
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,250
Is it five people or two people?

37
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,240
Two people or five people?

38
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,070
Five people or two people?

39
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:58,850
You're back?

40
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:00,080
We're back.

41
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,480
You sure you won't leave?

42
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:03,560
I promise I won't leave this time.

43
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,470
Wasn't it supposed to be Wuyaotian?

44
00:03:05,470 --> 00:03:06,930
Why did it become Wudiren?

45
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,190
Don't both of them
have a "Wu" in their names?

46
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:10,280
That counts?

47
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,700
Don't be angry.

48
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,150
C-Calm down.

49
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:20,490
What do you mean?

50
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,310
-You want another beating?
-You're still angry?

51
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,770
You want another beating?

52
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:23,800
Attention.

53
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:24,910
For our main visual effect,

54
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:26,400
switch it back immediately
after each song.

55
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:26,840
Okay?

56
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,910
And check the live and neutral wires

57
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:29,520
on all the speakers again.

58
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,560
Make sure you don't connect them wrong.

59
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,870
Okay? Come on. Get busy.

60
00:03:31,870 --> 00:03:32,520
Get moving.

61
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,590
Come on, come on.

62
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:38,400
Bingqiang has really changed a lot
since he was a kid.

63
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,930
He was short and chubby,
and he got bad grades.

64
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:42,680
Now, after spending some time
out in the world,

65
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,280
he seems to know everything.

66
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:45,630
Impressive.

67
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,590
It's all thanks to Bingqiang.

68
00:03:58,590 --> 00:03:59,190
Otherwise,

69
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,450
our village wouldn't be so lively.

70
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:01,100
Yeah.

71
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:03,820
Zhen.

72
00:04:04,430 --> 00:04:05,240
Actually,

73
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,710
about drums and music,

74
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:07,840
-I also...
-Zhen!

75
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,960
Come and do me a favor!

76
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,620
-I also have some...
-Coming!

77
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,080
Let's check the positions

78
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,000
of those two people from Wudiren.

79
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:13,840
Okay, stand over here.

80
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:14,840
Here. Stand here.

81
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,390
Are you upset,

82
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:18,750
Brother-in-law?

83
00:04:20,269 --> 00:04:21,529
Watch what you call me.

84
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,830
I haven't agreed to you and my sister
being together yet.

85
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:24,950
Wait a minute.

86
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:27,520
Move the microphone a little this way.

87
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:30,240
What is Bingqiang

88
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,600
showing off for?

89
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,000
He just wants to show off, right?

90
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:36,310
What a piece of trash.

91
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:40,560
Do you...

92
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,190
hate him that much?

93
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Brother-in-law.

94
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:49,870
I'll remind you of something
since you called me brother-in-law.

95
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:50,600
I'm all ears.

96
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,200
When we were young,
he fought with me over Zhen.

97
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,190
He played a lot of dirty tricks.

98
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:55,790
You should watch out for him.

99
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,040
What a piece of trash.

100
00:04:58,950 --> 00:05:00,410
Thanks, Brother-in-law.

101
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,930
Keep an eye on him for me.

102
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,560
Sure thing, Brother-in-law.

103
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,000
Thanks, Brother-in-law.

104
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,020
No problem, Brother-in-law.

105
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:06,680
Thanks, Brother-in-law.

106
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,430
My pleasure, Brother-in-law.

107
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:08,890
Thanks, Brother-in-law.

108
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,480
We're not on the same beat.

109
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:17,850
Get him.

110
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,950
Why are they singing?

111
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,530
But... they really look like
a perfect match.

112
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:29,850
Singing, huh?

113
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,150
He's pretty good at playing the accordion.

114
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:33,870
Dad.

115
00:05:34,390 --> 00:05:35,600
I heard you wrong.

116
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,360
You meant Liang Long?

117
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,040
I thought you said my aunt.

118
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,950
Mr. Liang is a good choice.

119
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,550
An absolutely great choice!

120
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:44,360
Isn't Mr. Liang a great choice?

121
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,330
Whatever...

122
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:52,040
♪ Whatever the outcome,
we won't back down ♪

123
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:55,630
♪ Choose happiness, not indifference ♪

124
00:05:56,630 --> 00:05:58,360
Do you think Mr. Liang

125
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,870
is still available now?

126
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,920
Why don't you do us a favor

127
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,250
and give a performance?

128
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,920
She's not looking for her aunt this time?

129
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,430
She's just a kid,

130
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:10,910
right?

131
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,390
Beg me.

132
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,960
This is really my first time.

133
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,160
Daddy!

134
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,450
It's for my kid's sake.

135
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,070
-Who is it?
-Hua.

136
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:29,830
Here are some things I want to say to you.

137
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,240
Mom, someone's looking for you!

138
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,740
Mom, someone's...

139
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,390
Who is it?

140
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:53,950
Mr. Uncle.

141
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,480
Well, have you finished your homework?

142
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,610
Go do your homework.

143
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,980
[Wudiren's Shapu Concert]

144
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:35,430
Thank you very much!

145
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:36,720
Thank you so much!

146
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:39,010
I want to give special thanks to someone.

147
00:07:39,070 --> 00:07:40,040
And that person is

148
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,600
Mr. Chen Bingqiang!

149
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:43,510
Bravo!

150
00:07:46,310 --> 00:07:47,720
Go, Bingqiang!

151
00:07:49,310 --> 00:07:50,000
Thank you!

152
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:52,070
Come on!

153
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,100
For our next song!

154
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,920
Let's get moving!

155
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:14,240
Water for sale!

156
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:15,560
Water!

157
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:16,890
Where's Zhou Ke?

158
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:18,070
Why aren't they with us?

159
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:19,870
This is the staff area.

160
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,360
If anything happens on stage,

161
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,120
we have to be the first

162
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,880
to rush up and solve the problem.

163
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,370
So you have to watch the stage carefully.

164
00:08:25,370 --> 00:08:26,630
Don't get distracted.

165
00:08:27,270 --> 00:08:27,830
Okay.

166
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:29,360
Ke, why aren't you going?

167
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:33,150
That's the staff boat.

168
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:34,000
They're all staff.

169
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,059
I don't have a pass.

170
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:36,669
For this concert,

171
00:08:37,549 --> 00:08:39,120
the staff, the stage—

172
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,440
everything was arranged by Bingqiang.

173
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,750
I didn't help at all,

174
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,840
so I'm embarrassed to go over there.

175
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,000
So what?

176
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,240
In my heart,

177
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,270
compared to him,

178
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,510
you are...

179
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,480
Alright, alright.

180
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,270
Anyway, in my heart,

181
00:08:56,270 --> 00:08:58,080
you're better than him, Ke.

182
00:08:58,270 --> 00:08:59,000
Thank you.

183
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:22,120
Zhen! Zhen!

184
00:09:22,630 --> 00:09:23,480
Come up!

185
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,270
You can see more clearly from here!

186
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:26,030
Come up!

187
00:09:26,050 --> 00:09:26,980
What did you say?

188
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,330
Thank you very much!

189
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:39,000
Okay!

190
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,670
The next song is great for dancing,

191
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,270
and also for falling in love.

192
00:09:43,510 --> 00:09:44,910
Come on! The next song!

193
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:46,870
Zhen Has a Crush on Qiang!

194
00:09:48,410 --> 00:09:49,190
[Zhen & Qiang]

195
00:09:54,910 --> 00:09:56,390
Cool!

196
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:03,870
Wudiren!

197
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:05,770
Well...

198
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,220
This Qiang doesn't mean Bingqiang.

199
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,420
They're not the same.

200
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,910
Zhen. Zhen.

201
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,150
Don't you think it's fate
that we're hearing this song?

202
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:18,870
This Bingqiang.

203
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:19,840
He did it on purpose.

204
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,640
He just had to arrange this song.

205
00:10:22,090 --> 00:10:24,690
This song is called
"Zhen Has a Crush on Qiang."

206
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,030
You're Zhen,

207
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,770
and I happen to be Qiang.

208
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,690
Why don't you also write a song?

209
00:10:30,550 --> 00:10:31,600
Write a song?

210
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:32,600
Are you kidding me?

211
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,800
It's not that simple.

212
00:10:34,270 --> 00:10:35,630
The one in the song is Qiang,

213
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:36,550
and you're Bingqiang.

214
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:37,480
How is that fate?

215
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,720
Right?

216
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,910
It's close enough.

217
00:10:41,230 --> 00:10:42,270
Write it tonight,

218
00:10:42,290 --> 00:10:44,020
and have them sing it tomorrow.

219
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:46,200
Zhen Has a Crush on Zhou Ke.

220
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:48,910
Zhou Ke sounds like Joker.

221
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:50,200
It's more fun.

222
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,400
It will definitely be better than this.

223
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:54,000
Alright?

224
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:56,830
You're going back to write the song, Ke?

225
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:00,960
Ke!

226
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,440
The concert in Shapu Village
is quite popular.

227
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:45,670
♪ Whatever the outcome,
we won't back down ♪

228
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,450
♪ Choose happiness, not indifference ♪

229
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:25,000
Blue sky.

230
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:27,070
White clouds.

231
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,500
Dried salted fish.

232
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:32,490
The waves bring back memories...

233
00:12:33,150 --> 00:12:33,960
from far away.

234
00:12:35,510 --> 00:12:37,500
Second Hand Pants is a piece of trash.

235
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:37,980
No.

236
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:40,960
It's a crappy punk...

237
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:42,510
band.

238
00:12:42,930 --> 00:12:44,960
The Death of Ma Long is a novel.

239
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:46,870
The Death of Marat...

240
00:12:47,910 --> 00:12:48,720
is a painting.

241
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:50,120
The Death of Mao...

242
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:51,390
is a plan.

243
00:12:51,910 --> 00:12:53,320
Well... I can't say this.

244
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:58,960
Bless me.

245
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,480
Let me make more money

246
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,320
and get rid of Renke soon.

247
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:05,730
I can only put up with him
for another half a year at most.

248
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,200
Mr. Renke.

249
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:10,750
My autograph. Take it.

250
00:13:10,750 --> 00:13:11,500
Thank you so much.

251
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,910
I'm the head of the

252
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,510
Culture and Tourism Department
in our village.

253
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:15,510
We've met before.

254
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,150
Um...

255
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:18,300
It's me.

256
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:20,390
Yes, um...

257
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:21,440
K-

258
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,150
Kawaii.

259
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,650
-Kawaii. Have a seat.
-You can also call me that.

260
00:13:24,650 --> 00:13:25,780
I bought some fruit.

261
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,390
Your performance last night was amazing.

262
00:13:29,390 --> 00:13:30,000
Really.

263
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,030
It was only a charity performance,

264
00:13:32,030 --> 00:13:32,600
but...

265
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,920
I'm always amazing on stage.

266
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,030
Charity performance?

267
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,750
Isn't it a charity performance?

268
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,000
Yes, it counts.

269
00:13:39,150 --> 00:13:41,960
Right, this probably counts
as a charity performance.

270
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:42,600
Mr. Mao.

271
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,710
Your performance yesterday was so lit.

272
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:46,870
Of course.

273
00:13:46,870 --> 00:13:48,150
We got paid for it.

274
00:13:48,750 --> 00:13:49,350
Of course.

275
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,270
Our villagers

276
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:52,000
really loved your performance.

277
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,200
After watching it yesterday,

278
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,000
they started a petition
that got 10,000 signatures.

279
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,720
Everyone hopes

280
00:13:57,150 --> 00:13:58,080
you'll sing only

281
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,750
"Zhen Has a Crush on Qiang" today.

282
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,320
On loop, all night.

283
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:02,530
I'd like to know

284
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,720
if you'll still sing

285
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,440
"Zhen Has a Crush on Qiang" tonight.

286
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,740
It's our signature song.

287
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:09,200
Even though it's a charity performance,
we'll definitely perform it.

288
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,730
Can you not sing it tonight?

289
